    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0267" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00/1040: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-10T15:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                                1921—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 11—12:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Department’s January 7, 5 p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d114-f1"/> Nicaraguan
                    Government the other day sent final instructions to its delegates to the effect
                    that it proposed to adhere strictly to its obligations in the Bryan–Chamorro
                        treaty<anchor n="25" xml:id="d114-f2"/> and the other Central American
                    States must accede to this, without reservation for future diplomatic
                    representations or arbitration, before Nicaragua will subscribe to Central
                    American Union Pact. Nicaraguan Government feels that it would jeopardize its
                    interests and would place it in a very false position with the United States to
                    do otherwise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
